ilure.verification_remediation` to `EVIDENCE_COLLECTION` only when existing test/verification evidence must be collected, or `TEST_CODE_CHANGE` when a test source change is required. Do not infer this from prose in downstream nodes. For REJECT, failure.category_hint is required and must be exactly one of [CONTRACT_GAP, CONTRACT_AMBIGUITY, IMPLEMENTATION_BUG, CONTEXT_INSUFFICIENT, VERIFICATION_INSUFFICIENT, TOOL_LIMITATION, REVIEW_NOISE]. No aliases or case normalization. For accepted decisions leave category_hint empty. Choose the repair owner: IMPLEMENTATION_BUG for product, documentation or test changes within the existing contract, including mixed repair and missing evidence; VERIFICATION_INSUFFICIENT only for collecting existing evidence. Contract categories require contract_gaps; all other categories forbid contract_gaps (existing-contract violations belong in must_fix). IMPLEMENTATION_BUG requires must_fix, out_of_scope_files or TEST_CODE_CHANGE. VERIFICATION_INSUFFICIENT requires missing_tests or missing_evidence and forbids context_gaps, out_of_scope_files and TEST_CODE_CHANGE. CONTEXT_INSUFFICIENT requires context_gaps; TOOL_LIMITATION requires failure.reason; both forbid out_of_scope_files and TEST_CODE_CHANGE. REVIEW_NOISE requires failure.reason, empty failure lists, empty must_fix/missing_evidence and NONE remediation. Contract categories may retain mixed issues. EVIDENCE_COLLECTION never overrides the category. TEST_CODE_CHANGE permits only implementation or contract categories. Successful self-test/acceptance must have one verification_checks entry for each approved criterion. Each entry contains exactly criterion_id, assertion, execution_ref, tool_call_ids, material_refs. assertion describes what the actual result demonstrates. execution_ref is CURRENT for this execution's program observations, or an exact prior verification-observations.json reference supplied in context; operator evidence uses the bound submission manifest. tool_call_ids may select